**Resubmitted: deviation (T4C), preferred-level cure.**

The only substantive change from the prior submission is wording that now uses the rule's own operative term: the inserted § 6(c) reads "Company may also terminate this Agreement or any Statement of Work **for convenience**, for any or no reason, upon thirty (30) days advance written notice…", which repairs the failed "Customer convenience termination present" check while retaining the contract's existing "for any or no reason" formulation.

All four preferred elements remain met in operative language by the single insertion:
1. Company convenience termination over the Agreement or any SOW;
2. 30 days' advance written notice;
3. pro-rata refund of prepaid fees for the post-termination period;
4. express bar on Contractor convenience termination while any SOW is outstanding.

§ 6(a)'s mutual 15-day right (available only when no SOW is outstanding) and § 6(b) breach mechanics survive verbatim; no extras, deletions, or dangling references were introduced.
